<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450356" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 5 — Bold used for Menu navigation sequence</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an HTML paragraph or procedural step that contains a menu navigation path such as</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>navigation</keyword>
        <keyword>sequence</keyword>
        <keyword>Bold</keyword>
        <keyword>Menu</keyword>
        <keyword>File</keyword>
        <keyword>Save</keyword>
        <indexterm>navigation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>sequence</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Bold</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider an HTML paragraph or procedural step that contains a menu navigation path such as "File → Save As", where each menu label is wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> element or the entire path is wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;span&gt;</codeph> element with a <codeph>&gt;</codeph> separator between menu labels.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Bold used for Menu navigation sequence</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;ol>
  &lt;li>
    Go to
    &lt;span class="menucascade">
      &lt;strong>File&lt;/strong> > &lt;strong>Save As&lt;/strong>
    &lt;/span>.
  &lt;/li>
&lt;/ol></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;taskbody>
  &lt;steps>
    &lt;step>
      &lt;cmd>
        Go to
        &lt;menucascade>
          &lt;uicontrol>File&lt;/uicontrol>
          &lt;uicontrol>Save As&lt;/uicontrol>
        &lt;/menucascade>.
      &lt;/cmd>
    &lt;/step>
  &lt;/steps>
&lt;/taskbody></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter detects the menu navigation pattern — multiple <codeph>&lt;strong&gt;</codeph> elements separated by a <codeph>&gt;</codeph> character within a <codeph>&lt;span&gt;</codeph> — and maps the sequence to a <codeph>&lt;menucascade&gt;</codeph> structure containing nested <codeph>&lt;uicontrol&gt;</codeph> elements.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
